REPAIRAGENT-OCI THOUGHTS: [0m The concrete cgroup retry problem is visible in mount_into_container: a failed mount is logged at error level before returning Err, but mount_cgroup_v2 intentionally treats that Err as a retry signal and falls back to a bind mount. This creates an error-level log for a recoverable path. A focused fix is to downgrade the helper's first-attempt mount log to debug, preserving the Err return so unrecoverable callers still report errors at their higher-level context. I will apply this line-oriented change with an explanatory comment and build it.
